#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:57
msgid ""
"The [public face](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage.h) "
"and [owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage_owner.h)"
" use exact instance/slot/epoch loans. Copying a token creates no new loan; "
"epochs never wrap. A live supported CPU/XIP/DMA-read loan excludes every "
"PROGRAM/ERASE writer to the entire aperture. All command, cache and DMA "
"writers must use the sole backend. Consumers join before release; failed "
"final unmap retains the exact loan and blocks writers. Stop permanently "
"closes admission and waits for all maps and the writer without revoking "
"them."
msgstr ""
"The [public face](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage.h) "
"and [owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage_owner.h)"
" use exact instance/slot/epoch loans. Copying a token creates no new loan; "
"epochs never wrap. A live supported CPU/XIP/DMA-read loan excludes every "
"PROGRAM/ERASE writer to the entire aperture. All command, cache and DMA "
"writers must use the sole backend. Consumers join before release; failed "
"final unmap retains the exact loan and blocks writers. Stop permanently "
"closes admission and waits for all maps and the writer without revoking "
"them."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:66
msgid ""
"Writer admission checks geometry, alignment, overflow and aliasing against "
"owner, slots, backend context and aperture before effects. Accepted PROGRAM "
"retains its input until settlement; partial effects remain visible and are "
"never replayed. After backend recovery, continued service can retry failed "
"drain. The [Native backend](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/native_mapped_storage.h)"
" preserves caller bytes, programs only 1-to-0, erases to `0xff` and mutates "
"at most the configured byte quantum per service call. It accepts coherent "
"CPU reads only. Physical QUADSPI/serial memory, SDMMC, XIP/cache/DMA "
"qualification and resource factory assembly remain open."
msgstr ""
"Writer admission checks geometry, alignment, overflow and aliasing against "
"owner, slots, backend context and aperture before effects. Accepted PROGRAM "
"retains its input until settlement; partial effects remain visible and are "
"never replayed. After backend recovery, continued service can retry failed "
"drain. The [Native backend](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/native_mapped_storage.h)"
" preserves caller bytes, programs only 1-to-0, erases to `0xff` and mutates "
"at most the configured byte quantum per service call. It accepts coherent "
"CPU reads only. Physical QUADSPI/serial memory, SDMMC, XIP/cache/DMA "
"qualification and resource factory assembly remain open."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:76
msgid "AMP epoch/cache lanes"
msgstr "AMP epoch/cache lanes"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:78
msgid ""
"The [AMP API](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc.h) and [caller-"
"storage constructor](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc_storage.h) use "
"separate offer and ACK cache lines, exact peer/local boot epochs and a "
"nonwrapping slot sequence. One serialized privileged Thread executes each "
"lane role. The caller supplies storage, coherent acquire/release control "
"access, cache clean/invalidate and a unique hardware-role claim. The "
"configured power-of-two cache granule is 1..64 B and divides 64 B. The claim"
" port rejects a reused or non-increasing local boot epoch, including after "
"normal join. Authoritative nonzero boot-epoch history must survive "
"CPU/whole-device resets and fail closed at exhaustion."
msgstr ""
"The [AMP API](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc.h) and [caller-"
"storage constructor](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc_storage.h) use "
"separate offer and ACK cache lines, exact peer/local boot epochs and a "
"nonwrapping slot sequence. One serialized privileged Thread executes each "
"lane role. The caller supplies storage, coherent acquire/release control "
"access, cache clean/invalidate and a unique hardware-role claim. The "
"configured power-of-two cache granule is 1..64 B and divides 64 B. The claim"
" port rejects a reused or non-increasing local boot epoch, including after "
"normal join. Authoritative nonzero boot-epoch history must survive "
"CPU/whole-device resets and fail closed at exhaustion."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:88
msgid ""
"Accepted send retains its payload until an acquire-observed exact epoch-"
"pair/sequence ACK or explicit proof that the old peer's CPU, DMA, IRQ and "
"observers can never again access the exact lane/payload under that execution"
" epoch. Elapsed timeouts never release a loan; observing a changed peer "
"epoch faults and closes the lane. Restoring an old shared word cannot reopen"
" it. Receive invalidates descriptors and payload before producing a readonly"
" view. The caller joins readers before `finish`; a valid `finish` consumes "
"that view even if ACK cache clean or epoch validation fails, while local "
"state remains retained for retry or recovery. `close` blocks admission; "
"`join` waits for ACKs and finished views; `reset_join` additionally requires"
" exact peer-stop proof. There is no cancel or blocking-wait API. Exact "
"multicore target, cache attributes, atomicity and resource partition are "
"unselected; single-core H743 is not an AMP target."
msgstr ""
"Accepted send retains its payload until an acquire-observed exact epoch-"
"pair/sequence ACK or explicit proof that the old peer's CPU, DMA, IRQ and "
"observers can never again access the exact lane/payload under that execution"
" epoch. Elapsed timeouts never release a loan; observing a changed peer "
"epoch faults and closes the lane. Restoring an old shared word cannot reopen"
" it. Receive invalidates descriptors and payload before producing a readonly"
" view. The caller joins readers before `finish`; a valid `finish` consumes "
"that view even if ACK cache clean or epoch validation fails, while local "
"state remains retained for retry or recovery. `close` blocks admission; "
"`join` waits for ACKs and finished views; `reset_join` additionally requires"
" exact peer-stop proof. There is no cancel or blocking-wait API. Exact "
"multicore target, cache attributes, atomicity and resource partition are "
"unselected; single-core H743 is not an AMP target."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:101
msgid "F407 masked tail handoff and clock barrier"
msgstr "F407 masked tail handoff and clock barrier"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:103
msgid ""
"The [handoff component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32f407_handoff/include/nexus/components/stm32f407_handoff.h)"
" reuses the existing ClockDomain barrier. Initialize once, explicitly enroll"
" every owner, close admission, cancel/drain/join all users, stop the actual "
"Platform and release exact leases. An empty foreign domain, stale epoch or "
"retained lease rejects. The domain cannot discover unenrolled users or other"
" bus masters."
msgstr ""
"The [handoff component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32f407_handoff/include/nexus/components/stm32f407_handoff.h)"
" reuses the existing ClockDomain barrier. Initialize once, explicitly enroll"
" every owner, close admission, cancel/drain/join all users, stop the actual "
"Platform and release exact leases. An empty foreign domain, stale epoch or "
"retained lease rejects. The domain cannot discover unenrolled users or other"
" bus masters."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:109
msgid ""
"The caller enters privileged MSP Thread with `PRIMASK=1`, "
"`BASEPRI=FAULTMASK=0` and `CONTROL=0`. It must establish stopped System, "
"HSI16/reset buses, no active FP/lazy context or MPU, no "
"enabled/pending/active SysTick/NVIC source, no live peripheral/DMA gate and "
"idle Flash with `ACR=0` (ART/prefetch disabled). Rejection preserves masks "
"and writes no MMIO; reading SysTick CTRL consumes COUNTFLAG. The 98-entry "
"Flash vector table is 512 B aligned and fits the exact generated/observed "
"512 KiB or 1 MiB density. MSP is 8 B aligned in `(0x20000000,0x20020000]`; "
"Thumb PC's first halfword lies in physical Flash. Shared device ID `0x413` "
"cannot establish exact-part/PCB identity. The caller excludes NMI/HardFault,"
" debugger and other masters throughout transfer."
msgstr ""
"The caller enters privileged MSP Thread with `PRIMASK=1`, "
"`BASEPRI=FAULTMASK=0` and `CONTROL=0`. It must establish stopped System, "
"HSI16/reset buses, no active FP/lazy context or MPU, no "
"enabled/pending/active SysTick/NVIC source, no live peripheral/DMA gate and "
"idle Flash with `ACR=0` (ART/prefetch disabled). Rejection preserves masks "
"and writes no MMIO; reading SysTick CTRL consumes COUNTFLAG. The 98-entry "
"Flash vector table is 512 B aligned and fits the exact generated/observed "
"512 KiB or 1 MiB density. MSP is 8 B aligned in `(0x20000000,0x20020000]`; "
"Thumb PC's first halfword lies in physical Flash. Shared device ID `0x413` "
"cannot establish exact-part/PCB identity. The caller excludes NMI/HardFault,"
" debugger and other masters throughout transfer."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:120
msgid ""
"Successful tail transfer never returns: it sets VTOR, disables CP10/11 with "
"barriers, clears CONTROL/PSP, replaces MSP and branches while masked. Main "
"SRAM persists until target startup. The target accepts masked entry and "
"resets controllers before enabling gates; no source deadline survives. Image"
" selection, authentication, partitions and recovery stay external. Live "
"RTOS/FPU adoption, H743/cache handoff, DVFS and deep-STOP continuity remain "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Successful tail transfer never returns: it sets VTOR, disables CP10/11 with "
"barriers, clears CONTROL/PSP, replaces MSP and branches while masked. Main "
"SRAM persists until target startup. The target accepts masked entry and "
"resets controllers before enabling gates; no source deadline survives. Image"
" selection, authentication, partitions and recovery stay external. Live "
"RTOS/FPU adoption, H743/cache handoff, DVFS and deep-STOP continuity remain "
"open."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:127
msgid "U575 retained LSE calendar in RUN"
msgstr "U575 retained LSE calendar in RUN"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:129
msgid ""
"The [RTC provider](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32u575/drivers/rtc.c) requires an external"
" boot owner to preserve a valid 24-hour BCD calendar, `BYPSHAD`, prescalers "
"127/255, actual LSE 32768 Hz, `RTCSEL=LSE`, `RTCEN`, `LSERDY`, `RTCAPBEN`, "
"`PWREN` and `DBP`. Boot hands over locked WPR; it remains locked between "
"calls with no other writer. Calibration, shift, binary mode, another RTC "
"owner and a live RTC vector reject. Accepted service briefly unlocks WPR "
"with CA/53, checks the protected write and unconditionally relocks with FF. "
"The provider does not write calendar, RCC, PWR or TAMP, enable an IRQ or "
"repair/reset the backup domain. Year-00 provenance remains external; INITS "
"cannot prove it. `set` returns `UNSUPPORTED`."
msgstr ""
"The [RTC provider](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32u575/drivers/rtc.c) requires an external"
" boot owner to preserve a valid 24-hour BCD calendar, `BYPSHAD`, prescalers "
"127/255, actual LSE 32768 Hz, `RTCSEL=LSE`, `RTCEN`, `LSERDY`, `RTCAPBEN`, "
"`PWREN` and `DBP`. Boot hands over locked WPR; it remains locked between "
"calls with no other writer. Calibration, shift, binary mode, another RTC "
"owner and a live RTC vector reject. Accepted service briefly unlocks WPR "
"with CA/53, checks the protected write and unconditionally relocks with FF. "
"The provider does not write calendar, RCC, PWR or TAMP, enable an IRQ or "
"repair/reset the backup domain. Year-00 provenance remains external; INITS "
"cannot prove it. `set` returns `UNSUPPORTED`."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:140
msgid ""
"ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.2.3 and 2.2.16 identify oscillator-stop limitations "
"for LSE drive codes 00/01 on revision X; Table 3 marks these limitations "
"repaired on W/U. This reference does not qualify a silicon revision, so its "
"crystal-mode profile requires `LSEBYP=0` and conservatively admits only "
"`LSEDRV=10/11` on every revision. It never writes either field. Section "
"2.2.1 separately requires external boot and Board owners to exclude PC13 "
"transitions for crystal LSE on this LQFP part. LSE bypass is unaffected by "
"section 2.2.1 and is outside this selected profile. GPIO reads cannot prove "
"that electrical condition, and this software reference declares no PCB route"
" or measured oscillator behavior."
msgstr ""
"ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.2.3 and 2.2.16 identify oscillator-stop limitations "
"for LSE drive codes 00/01 on revision X; Table 3 marks these limitations "
"repaired on W/U. This reference does not qualify a silicon revision, so its "
"crystal-mode profile requires `LSEBYP=0` and conservatively admits only "
"`LSEDRV=10/11` on every revision. It never writes either field. Section "
"2.2.1 separately requires external boot and Board owners to exclude PC13 "
"transitions for crystal LSE on this LQFP part. LSE bypass is unaffected by "
"section 2.2.1 and is outside this selected profile. GPIO reads cannot prove "
"that electrical condition, and this software reference declares no PCB route"
" or measured oscillator behavior."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:150
msgid ""
"Reads try at most eight coherent SSR/TR/DR pairs and preserve output on "
"invalid or unstable data. Natural year 99-to-00 rollover preserves the "
"domain; successful reopen advances a nonwrapping 64-bit domain. AlarmA "
"borrows one request. Core monotonic deadlines remain independent of calendar"
" time. One service phase per call disables ALRAE with readback and a 100 µs "
"Core-time crossing guard, clears and observes ALRAF, then restores saved "
"alarm registers with readback before detaching and settling. Failed "
"disable/clear/restore retains quarantine. Foreign clock/configuration drift "
"permanently retains responsibility for external recovery. This mode provides"
" no Stop2, LPDMA, VBAT-continuity or wake qualification."
msgstr ""
"Reads try at most eight coherent SSR/TR/DR pairs and preserve output on "
"invalid or unstable data. Natural year 99-to-00 rollover preserves the "
"domain; successful reopen advances a nonwrapping 64-bit domain. AlarmA "
"borrows one request. Core monotonic deadlines remain independent of calendar"
" time. One service phase per call disables ALRAE with readback and a 100 µs "
"Core-time crossing guard, clears and observes ALRAF, then restores saved "
"alarm registers with readback before detaching and settling. Failed "
"disable/clear/restore retains quarantine. Foreign clock/configuration drift "
"permanently retains responsibility for external recovery. This mode provides"
" no Stop2, LPDMA, VBAT-continuity or wake qualification."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:160
