#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:162
msgid ""
"The [frame contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/frame_stream.h) binds a copied, "
"checked layout to an existing `nx_stream` pool. Audio layouts retain full "
"stored slots, including inactive SAI slots; PDM uses byte-interleaved lanes "
"and complete eight-frame groups. Planar layouts accept up to four disjoint "
"checked stride intervals. These are data contracts, not SAI/DCMI providers. "
"Publication requires complete frame bytes. Empty acquisition increments a "
"saturating underrun counter without choosing silence/repeat policy. DMA-view"
" release requires actual engine, IRQ and peripheral detachment facts and "
"exact control identity/epoch."
msgstr ""
"The [frame contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/frame_stream.h) binds a copied, "
"checked layout to an existing `nx_stream` pool. Audio layouts retain full "
"stored slots, including inactive SAI slots; PDM uses byte-interleaved lanes "
"and complete eight-frame groups. Planar layouts accept up to four disjoint "
"checked stride intervals. These are data contracts, not SAI/DCMI providers. "
"Publication requires complete frame bytes. Empty acquisition increments a "
"saturating underrun counter without choosing silence/repeat policy. DMA-view"
" release requires actual engine, IRQ and peripheral detachment facts and "
"exact control identity/epoch."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:171
msgid ""
"The [DMA2D component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h743_frame_dma2d/include/nexus/components/frame_dma2d.h)"
" has one caller-owned executor and no queue. It admits exact H743 V ID "
"`0x20030450`, D-Cache off and exclusive cold DMA2D. The two request formats "
"are RGB565 copy (the zero value) and fixed ARGB8888-to-RGB565 pixel format "
"conversion (PFC). Unknown formats are rejected; CLUT, blending, other "
"formats and IRQ operation remain unsupported. Both surfaces must occupy AXI "
"SRAM `[0x24000000,0x24080000)`. No Board connection or physical result is "
"inferred."
msgstr ""
"The [DMA2D component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h743_frame_dma2d/include/nexus/components/frame_dma2d.h)"
" has one caller-owned executor and no queue. It admits exact H743 V ID "
"`0x20030450`, D-Cache off and exclusive cold DMA2D. The two request formats "
"are RGB565 copy (the zero value) and fixed ARGB8888-to-RGB565 pixel format "
"conversion (PFC). Unknown formats are rejected; CLUT, blending, other "
"formats and IRQ operation remain unsupported. Both surfaces must occupy AXI "
"SRAM `[0x24000000,0x24080000)`. No Board connection or physical result is "
"inferred."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:179
msgid ""
"`x` and `width_bytes` always count source bytes. Source addresses, x, widths"
" and strides align to two bytes for RGB565 or four for ARGB8888. ARGB8888 "
"input on this little-endian MCU stores B, G, R, A bytes; RGB565 discards "
"alpha with no channel or byte swap. Output addresses and strides align to "
"two bytes; output row bytes equal `width_bytes / source_pixel_bytes * 2`. "
"Destination stride and capacity remain bytes. With `LOM=0`, foreground and "
"output offsets count their own format's pixels: source padding divided by "
"four for PFC or two for copy, and output padding divided by two. Each pixel "
"gap is at most `0x3fff`; bits 15:14 are ignored in pixel mode despite the "
"16-bit register field (RM0433 Rev9, sections 18.5.5 and 18.5.20). Width is "
"at most `0x3fff` pixels and height at most `0xffff` rows. Successful request"
" results report output bytes without stride padding. Arithmetic, AXI spans "
"and hardware bounds are checked before acceptance."
msgstr ""
"`x` and `width_bytes` always count source bytes. Source addresses, x, widths"
" and strides align to two bytes for RGB565 or four for ARGB8888. ARGB8888 "
"input on this little-endian MCU stores B, G, R, A bytes; RGB565 discards "
"alpha with no channel or byte swap. Output addresses and strides align to "
"two bytes; output row bytes equal `width_bytes / source_pixel_bytes * 2`. "
"Destination stride and capacity remain bytes. With `LOM=0`, foreground and "
"output offsets count their own format's pixels: source padding divided by "
"four for PFC or two for copy, and output padding divided by two. Each pixel "
"gap is at most `0x3fff`; bits 15:14 are ignored in pixel mode despite the "
"16-bit register field (RM0433 Rev9, sections 18.5.5 and 18.5.20). Width is "
"at most `0x3fff` pixels and height at most `0xffff` rows. Successful request"
" results report output bytes without stride padding. Arithmetic, AXI spans "
"and hardware bounds are checked before acceptance."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:193
msgid ""
"Destination writes and every ownership control must be disjoint from every "
"source-pool slot's full capacity, including frame tails and other free "
"slots. Admission scans the bounded pool in O(n), comparing seven fixed "
"controls per slot. Acceptance borrows the request, exact live source-frame "
"loan and output; the selected source slot remains immutable through final "
"access. Rejection leaves the original source loan with its caller. Submit "
"`SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED, including a subsequent setup/readback failure; "
"such a failure keeps all borrows until service proves drain. The first "
"observed failure remains latched across cancellation and recoverable "
"cache/IRQ guard restoration."
msgstr ""
"Destination writes and every ownership control must be disjoint from every "
"source-pool slot's full capacity, including frame tails and other free "
"slots. Admission scans the bounded pool in O(n), comparing seven fixed "
"controls per slot. Acceptance borrows the request, exact live source-frame "
"loan and output; the selected source slot remains immutable through final "
"access. Rejection leaves the original source loan with its caller. Submit "
"`SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED, including a subsequent setup/readback failure; "
"such a failure keeps all borrows until service proves drain. The first "
"observed failure remains latched across cancellation and recoverable "
"cache/IRQ guard restoration."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:203
msgid ""
"Successful completion requires TC and START-clear. Cancel/error drain "
"instead requires START/CLUT/IRQ withdrawal without requiring TC. START and "
"ABORT writes preserve the selected mode. START is a read/set bit: writing "
"zero has no effect. ABORT requests hardware withdrawal without reasserting a"
" previously cleared START. The provider releases the loan only after the "
"hardware proof and clearing FGMAR/OMAR/NLR. Failed proof retains every "
"borrow in quarantine; continued service can recover an actual drain. If an "
"active owner observes its required RCC gate off or DMA2D reset asserted, "
"transfer history is uncertain and quarantine is permanent: restoring "
"registers to zero cannot revoke the borrow, and service, stop or "
"reinitialization cannot reclaim it. An unobserved reset pulse is not "
"detectable; exclusive gate/reset ownership remains a mandatory precondition."
" System-level recovery stays external. Stop closes admission and returns "
"`BUSY` for active work; only after all loans settle does it reset the "
"controller and withdraw its owned gate. These software and ELF checks "
"establish no PFC throughput, latency or HIL result."
msgstr ""
"Successful completion requires TC and START-clear. Cancel/error drain "
"instead requires START/CLUT/IRQ withdrawal without requiring TC. START and "
"ABORT writes preserve the selected mode. START is a read/set bit: writing "
"zero has no effect. ABORT requests hardware withdrawal without reasserting a"
" previously cleared START. The provider releases the loan only after the "
"hardware proof and clearing FGMAR/OMAR/NLR. Failed proof retains every "
"borrow in quarantine; continued service can recover an actual drain. If an "
"active owner observes its required RCC gate off or DMA2D reset asserted, "
"transfer history is uncertain and quarantine is permanent: restoring "
"registers to zero cannot revoke the borrow, and service, stop or "
"reinitialization cannot reclaim it. An unobserved reset pulse is not "
"detectable; exclusive gate/reset ownership remains a mandatory precondition."
" System-level recovery stays external. Stop closes admission and returns "
"`BUSY` for active work; only after all loans settle does it reset the "
"controller and withdraw its owned gate. These software and ELF checks "
"establish no PFC throughput, latency or HIL result."

